  "label": "Interracial couple mapped as 'farm equipment and livestock'",
  "description": "The text 'farm equipment and livestock don't mix' is used as a crude metaphor to imply that the interracial couple (Black man and white woman) is an unnatural or unsuitable pairing. This creates an analogical mapping where the couple is projected onto the metaphorical entities 'farm equipment' and 'livestock', suggesting biological or social incompatibility.",
